{
 "text": "Here are two words that differ in a single letter: Hello with a capital H, and hello with a lowercase one. Their inline C-I-Ds differ in a single character, which makes sense. The C-I-D is just the word, re-encoded.\n\nNow here are their Shaw five-twelve fingerprints. Not one family resemblance. Line up the bits and count, and two hundred and thirty-nine of the five hundred and twelve bits are different. Very close to half. Which is exactly what you'd expect if the two outputs were completely unrelated random numbers.\n\nThat's not a quirk of this example. It's the whole design goal. Last time we treated this fingerprint as a black box. Today we open the box, at least a little, and ask a precise question: what exactly is it promising?",
